Part I - English (governing text)
=================================

1. Definitions

"RokBot" means the project published at https://github.com/hongfaqiu/rokbot.

"Covered Material" means the work of the RokBot contributors in this
repository and in RokBot distributions: source code, patch recipes, scripts,
documentation, images, and any compiled or packaged form of that work, in both
public and private distributions, including RokBot changes that end up inside
a patched application or a container image.

"Noncommercial" means not primarily intended for or directed toward commercial
advantage or monetary compensation, whether direct or indirect.

2. What this license does not cover

(a) Original Grok Bot programs. The official Grok Bot clients, installers,
    bundles and services are not part of the Covered Material. This license
    grants nothing in them; their own license terms and terms of service apply.

(b) Trademarks. Grok, Grok Bot, RokBot and any other names, logos and marks
    are not licensed by this document.

(c) Third-party components. Components identified as coming from a third party
    (for example in a THIRD_PARTY file, a bundled node_modules directory, or a
    file header) remain under their own licenses and notices. This license
    neither adds rights to them nor limits rights their own licenses give you
    when you use them on their own.

(d) Upstream portions. Parts of RokBot derive from ProkBot and ProkBot Plus.
    Those portions also remain subject to the ProkBot Noncommercial License
    1.0, kept unchanged in LICENSES/ProkBot-Noncommercial-1.0.txt, and to the
    notices listed in NOTICE. Where both licenses apply, you must comply with
    both.

3. What you may do

You may, for Noncommercial purposes only:

- use, run and self-host the Covered Material for yourself;
- study it, learn from it, and use it in Noncommercial research;
- copy and modify it and make derivative works;
- share public distributions and your modified versions with others,
  free of charge.

When you share copies or modified versions you must: include this license and
NOTICE; keep the copyright, upstream and third-party notices; mark clearly what
you changed; and pass the same Noncommercial terms on to recipients. You may
not offer the Covered Material, or any derivative of it, under terms that
permit commercial use.

4. What you may not do

Commercial use of any kind is not licensed. In particular you may not:

- sell, rent or license the Covered Material, patches, patched applications,
  container images or derivative works for a fee;
- offer paid hosting, SaaS, subscriptions, API access, managed deployment,
  installation, customization, support or any other paid service based on it;
- build it into a commercial product or service, or use it to deliver paid
  work to clients;
- use it in the operations or projects of a business, even if no one is
  charged for access to it;
- earn money from access or use through advertising, bundling or similar
  arrangements.

Renaming the project, changing its code, or collecting payment through someone
else does not make a commercial use permitted.

5. Private distributions

A distribution that its README or release manifest marks as "private" may be
used, copied and modified only by collaborators the repository owner has
expressly authorized. You may not pass it outside that group, publish it, or
offer it for public download. This is in addition to the Noncommercial
conditions. A public edition you obtain independently is governed by section 3.

6. Termination

Your rights under this license end automatically if you break any of its terms.
Rights not expressly granted here are reserved.

7. No warranty; limitation of liability

THE COVERED MATERIAL IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS
OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR
PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE
AUTHORS AND COPYRIGHT HOLDERS ARE NOT LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
LIABILITY ARISING FROM THE COVERED MATERIAL OR ITS USE. YOU ARE RESPONSIBLE
FOR HOW YOU USE IT AND FOR COMPLYING WITH APPLICABLE LAW AND THIRD-PARTY RIGHTS.


Part II - 简体中文（参考译文，以英文版为准）
=========================================

RokBot 非商业许可证 1.0
版权所有 (c) 2026 RokBot contributors

本中文文本仅供参考。中英文本如有不一致，以上方英文版为准。

1. 定义
「RokBot」指发布于 https://github.com/hongfaqiu/rokbot 的项目。
「受许可内容」指 RokBot 贡献者在本仓库及 RokBot 发行包中的成果，包括源代码、
补丁配方、脚本、文档、图片及其编译或打包形式；公开版与私有版均适用，也包括
进入补丁后应用或容器镜像中的 RokBot 修改。
「非商业」指主要目的不在于直接或间接获取商业利益或金钱报酬。

2. 不在本许可范围内的内容
(a) 原版 Grok Bot 程序：官方客户端、安装包、界面包和服务不属于受许可内容，
    本许可不授予其任何权利，仍适用其自身许可条款和服务条款。
(b) 商标：Grok、Grok Bot、RokBot 等名称、标志和商标不因本许可获得授权。
(c) 第三方组件：经标明来自第三方的组件（如 THIRD_PARTY 文件、随附的
    node_modules 目录或文件头所示）继续适用其自身许可和声明。本许可不增加
    对它们的权利，也不限制其原许可允许的独立使用。
(d) 上游部分：RokBot 的部分内容衍生自 ProkBot 和 ProkBot Plus，这些部分同时
    继续受 ProkBot Noncommercial License 1.0（原文保留于
    LICENSES/ProkBot-Noncommercial-1.0.txt）及 NOTICE 所列声明约束。两份
    许可同时适用时，须同时遵守。

3. 允许的使用（仅限非商业目的）
- 个人使用、运行和自部署自用；
- 学习、研究，以及非商业研究用途；
- 复制、修改和制作衍生作品；
- 免费向他人分享公开版及你的修改版本。
分享副本或修改版时，须附带本许可证和 NOTICE，保留版权、上游及第三方声明，
清楚注明你的修改，并让接收者同样受非商业条件约束；不得以允许商用的条款
提供受许可内容或其衍生作品。

4. 禁止的使用
本许可不授权任何商业用途，包括但不限于：收费出售、出租或授权软件、补丁、
补丁后应用、容器镜像或衍生作品；基于本软件提供付费托管、SaaS、订阅、API、
托管部署、安装、定制、支持等付费服务；集成到商业产品或服务，或用于为客户
完成付费工作；用于企业经营或商业项目（即使不对访问单独收费）；通过广告、
捆绑等方式变现。更名、修改代码或经由第三方收费，均不改变上述限制。

5. 私有发行版
README 或发行清单标注为「private」的发行版，仅限仓库所有者明确授权的协作者
使用、复制和修改，不得外传、公开发布或提供公开下载，并同样受非商业条件约束。
独立取得的公开版适用第 3 条。

6. 终止
违反本许可任一条款，你在本许可下的权利自动终止。未明确授予的权利均予保留。

7. 免责与责任限制
受许可内容按「现状」提供，不附带任何明示或默示担保，包括适销性、特定用途
适用性及不侵权担保。在适用法律允许的范围内，作者和版权人不对因受许可内容
或其使用产生的任何索赔、损害或其他责任负责。使用者须自行承担使用责任，并
遵守适用法律及第三方权利。
